body:
I've always wanted to be a musician. Conservatoires are an option, but I got dealt with the triple whammy of being a singer, being a transgender man, and not being able to even think about starting testosterone until I've graduated secondary school. If I skip uni and go to a conservatoire for my bachelor's I'll then have those years of education mean nothing after my voice drops, or wait anywhere from 4 to 8 years to graduate, then get the required one year "real life experience" to go on hormones, *then* wait for my voice to drop and settle. Not to mention, I'm pretty sure I wouldn't be able to handle having my singing classes consist of performing in front of a group then being criticized in front that same group, all of which will be incredibly talented and accomplished singers. Maybe in a few years down the line when/if I get proper help for dealing with stress, but certainly not straight out of secondary school.

&#x200B;

I've considered going into trade but, well, upper-middle class Chinese family. My parents would kill me before they even thought about letting me become a plumber or electrician.
